Subject: termio: stop CSIData::readFrom writing one past
 _separators

A CSI sequence with maxLength or more ';'/':' separators wrote _separators[maxLength - 1],
one past the end of the array. The sequence is now rejected, as an over-long sequence
already is.
---
 source/platform/termio.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/source/platform/termio.cpp b/source/platform/termio.cpp
index 9d943bc..81f9e13 100644
--- a/source/platform/termio.cpp
+++ b/source/platform/termio.cpp
@@ -261,7 +261,13 @@ bool CSIData::readFrom(GetChBuf &buf) noexcept
             // No more input and CSI is not yet complete.
             return false;
         if (k == ';' || k == ':')
+        {
+            // _separators has room for maxLength - 1 entries; a CSI sequence with
+            // maxLength or more parameters would write one past its end.
+            if (i + 1 == maxLength)
+                return false;
             _separators[i] = (char) k;
+        }
         else
         {
             terminator = (char) k;
